  "finding": {
    "type": "gap - designer decision",
    "detail": "The four lighting-related tier settings (localLights, smallPartShadows, cameraDoF, ambientLife) are declared in FidelityTier.SETTINGS, returned by FidelityRuntime.settings(), and mirrored to the player FidelityTier attribute, but no consumer applies them to Lighting or to local light/effect instances. Sky.luau alone owns Lighting post effects (seasons/weather driven, not tier driven). cameraDoF=true on Tinggi created no DepthOfFieldEffect (dof=0 in every row). Hub-local light/effect counts were identical across all three tiers at every hub. No tier switch creates or destroys any Lighting effect, so none can be left stuck on. Wiring tier->lighting is a designer look decision (VISUAL_MASTER_PLAN V0.4 still BLOCKED); recorded under WORK_QUEUE 'Decisions for designer'."
  },
